From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:39:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D302 tui: --continue with no session opens home

Upstream: `--continue` starts on a placeholder session route ("dummy") until the latest session is known. With no session to continue the route is never left: the TUI loads the placeholder as a session, which fails server-side validation, so it shows a raw validation-error toast (`Expected a string starting with "ses"`, whichever invalid request fails first) before falling back to home. With sessions, the placeholder's failing requests race the real navigation.
Fixed: the placeholder is never loaded as a session (no requests for it); with nothing to continue, or when listing/forking fails, the TUI goes home (the failure still toasts).
Scenarios: tui/nav-args.test.ts "args: --continue without any session", "args: --continue opens the latest session" (new)
Upstream tests: test/app-lifecycle.test.tsx: the sessions it opens are no longer named "dummy", the placeholder's reserved ID

